# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings, on every platform.
# Git for Windows rewrites text files to CRLF by default, and the policy
# tests in crates/wallet-core/tests/policy.rs read sources and manifests as
# bytes; a CRLF checkout would be a tree that is not the commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The reference renderings are PNG captures of the frames of the owner's
# HTML bundle, which is not committed (docs/DECISIONS.md D14,
# design/INDEX.md). They are never edited (docs/PLAN.md section 5: "Do not
# edit them"), so git never converts them, whatever their content looks like.
design/renderings/** -text

# Font binaries are vendored files, kept byte for byte as published. Their
# licence texts get a rule of their own, by directory, when the fonts are
# added (phase 3): a licence file's name varies by foundry.
*.ttf -text
*.otf -text
*.woff2 -text
